scandump (2.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Package the scanner merged in #10.
  * Add -i/--interval to wait a number of seconds between scans. The
    default stays 0, so a run with no new flags still scans continuously.
  * Behavior change: beacon frames keep every information element. Large
    Wi-Fi 6E and Wi-Fi 7 beacons were cut off at 2048 bytes. The PCAP
    snapshot length is 262144.
  * Behavior change: networks with no dBm signal, and networks with a
    beacon interval of 0, are written. Both used to be dropped.
  * Behavior change: 5 GHz channel 177 (5885 MHz) gets radiotap channel
    flags. Flags follow the band edges.
  * Behavior change: giving up after 30 transient failures exits 240.
  * Behavior change: if the program reading standard output closes the
    pipe, scandump stops with status 0. A write error, such as a full
    disk, exits non-zero.
  * Behavior change: the package no longer installs
    /etc/sudoers.d/scandump. The same rule is an example at
    /usr/share/doc/scandump/examples/sudoers. A rule already on disk stays
    across the upgrade.
  * -V is a short form of --version. The version line reads
    "scandump version 2.3.0". A fatal scan error is followed by a hint
    for the common causes. scandump(8) documents the exit statuses.

 -- jsz <josh@joshschmelzle.com>  Sun, 25 Oct 2026 16:45:19 +0000

scandump (2.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ignore scan events for other interfaces so a scan started by another
    process (e.g. wpa_supplicant) is no longer reported as an aborted scan.

 -- Adrian Granados <adrian@intuitibits.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 20:55:10 +0000

scandump (2.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix an indefinite wait when the kernel rejects the scan trigger (e.g.
    -EBUSY while another process is scanning) instead of retrying.
  * Add a receive timeout and SIGINT/SIGTERM handling so a stuck driver or
    Ctrl-C can no longer hang the process.
  * Validate the BSSID attribute length before copying it into the packet
    buffer.
  * Check the previously-unchecked netlink calls and bound the transient
    error retry loop.
  * Reject invalid, out-of-range and duplicate values for -c and -f, and
    report a clear error for an unknown interface name.
  * Refuse to follow a symlink at the output path. File permissions are
    unchanged, matching tcpdump (0666 as masked by umask).
  * Build with -O2 and honor the environment's CFLAGS/CPPFLAGS/LDFLAGS so
    the package build's hardening flags are applied.

 -- Adrian Granados <adrian@intuitibits.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 16:55:32 +0000

